  "@id": "https://pices-data.github.io/odis/records/zenodo-23519456.jsonld",
  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Surface Marine Data",
  "description": "Synoptic observations taken aboard ships of opportunity, research vessels, and navy ships. All standard surface meteorological elements are recorded. In addition, sea surface temperature, ice accretion, and wave direction/height are most often observed. The data set contains observations received from Global Telecommunications System (GTS) international exchange and ships logs. Observations usually taken at 4 main GMT synoptic hours but some 3-hourly intermediate observations also are included. Recent (1970's) adjunct data set contains permanent and drifting buoy data (TD-1132). Data consists of approximately 328 reels CCT at 6250 bpi and the bytes per record are variable.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To create a data set containing observations received from Global Telecommunications System (GTS) international exchange and ships logs.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23519457",
